docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T72.md:39:7. Add inbox-specific i18n keys to `extension/src/review/i18n/en.json` under a `memoryInbox` namespace: column headers, filter labels, empty-state message ("No memories match the current filters."), error-state message, loading skeleton hint, and per-status badge labels (already partly present from T71; reuse keys instead of forking).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T72.md:41:9. Wrap every bridge call in `try/catch`. On error, render the inline error banner from T71 and call `vscode.window.showErrorMessage(err.message)` so the error is visible at both surfaces.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T72.md:72:- Sortable tables use `SortableHeader` + `useTableSort` equivalents exposed by T71's scaffolding; the inbox table sorts on `Status`, `Class`, `Scope`, `Last Verified`, and `Confidence` columns.
