docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:882:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019ScAFhwj15KgrT4jB8Uvi8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012LWeY2EjcfBk7ufhaBmdDS","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T85.md","content":"# T85 — Phase 11 — Documentation suite (all 11 required docs from spec §Documentation Requirements)\n\n**Phase:** 11\n**Type:** docs\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R47, R54, R63, R70, R78\n**Spec anchor:** [§Documentation Requirements](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#documentation-requirements), [§Phase 11: Hardening](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-11-hardening)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task delivers the complete documentation suite Phase 11 mandates. Spec §Documentation Requirements lists eleven required documents: successor architecture overview, MCP contract reference (which T61 was responsible for; this task collects/links it), memory model reference, event log design, consolidation design, retrieval/ranking design, verification/freshness design, operator guide, migration guide from Lattice, benchmark/evaluation guide, extension review UI guide. Spec §Phase 11 DoD includes \"documentation for setup, operations, memory semantics, and workflow behavior\"; this task closes the documentation surface area so the system is \"production-grade for repeated agent use, not only successful on a toy repo.\"\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Required docs: successor architecture overview; MCP contract reference; memory model reference; event log design; consolidation design; retrieval/ranking design; verification/freshness design; operator guide; migration guide from Lattice; benchmark/evaluation guide; extension review UI guide.\" (spec §Documentation Requirements)\n\n> \"Docs must be updated in the same change as public behavior changes.\" (spec §Documentation Requirements)\n\n> \"Phase 11 DoD: the system is production-grade for repeated agent use, not only successful on a toy repo.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R47 (Phase 6 consolidation), R54 (Phase 7 verification), R63 (Phase 8 workflow + memory tools including the MCP contract reference from T61), R70 (Phase 9 metrics + benchmarks), R78 (Phase 10 review UI).\n- Existing architecture docs this suite must reference (not duplicate):\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md` (T02)\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` (T02)\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md` (T03)\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-storage-migration-policy.md` (T03)\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-event-log-compaction.md` (assumed from T16)\n  - Plus any MCP contract reference produced in Phase 8 from T61.\n  - Plus all `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-*.md` legacy docs (referenced by heading, not duplicated).\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` (no broken windows, single source of truth — every concept lives in exactly one doc); `lattice/CLAUDE.md` (Markdown heading references).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Documentation Requirements in full so the eleven required documents are pinned. Cross-reference each with the existing architecture docs to identify which ones are net-new vs. consolidation-of-existing.\n2. Create `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-successor-architecture-overview.md`. This is the front-door doc operators read first. Required headings: `## Overview`, `## Three substrates`, `## Identity model`, `## Storage layout`, `## Read paths`, `## Write paths`, `## Operational invariants`. Reference but do not duplicate the per-substrate design docs created below.\n3. Create `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-model-reference.md`. The authoritative reference for the memory graph. Required headings: `## Memory classes` (all classes from spec §4 including `CounterMemory`), `## Memory record fields` (every field from spec §4 with type, nullability, default), `## Memory link types` (all link types from spec §4 with reciprocity rules), `## Scope semantics` (session / branch / repo / user / organization), `## Verification status state machine`, `## Freshness policy`, `## Validity conditions and invalidation triggers`, `## Memory evidence`, `## Memory access history and usefulness scores`.\n4. Create `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-event-log-design.md`. The authoritative reference for the event log. Required headings: `## Append-only invariant`, `## Event kinds` (all 20 from spec §3), `## Event envelope` (every field from spec §3), `## Payload spillover`, `## Compaction snapshots`, `## Replay semantics`, `## Hot-path budgets`, `## Workspace and session scoping`.\n5. Create `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-design.md`. The authoritative reference for the consolidation engine. Required headings: `## Job types`, `## Modes` (synchronous / background / manual-review / replay), `## LLM-driven consolidation` (proposal-only, provenance, queue depth, cost budgets per spec §6), `## Proposal apply and reject flow`, `## Reversibility`, `## Replay-safe execution`.\n6. Create `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-retrieval-ranking-design.md`. The authoritative reference for retrieval. Required headings: `## Pipeline` (the ten-step pipeline from spec §7), `## Candidate sources`, `## Ranking signals` (all 13 from spec §7), `## Diagnostic mode`, `## Compact mode`, `## Inclusion reasons and expansion handles`, `## Forward compatibility with working memory`.\n7. Create `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-verification-freshness-design.md`. The authoritative reference for verification. Required headings: `## Verification checks` (every check from spec §8), `## Verification outputs` (all eight statuses from spec §8), `## Incremental verification`, `## Graph-change triggers`, `## Branch and workspace scope enforcement`, `## Time-bound expiry`.\n8. Create `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-operator-guide.md`. Operator-facing how-to. Required headings: `## Installation`, `## Initial setup`, `## Daily operations`, `## Review surface tour` (cross-link to the extension UI guide), `## Metrics dashboard`, `## Troubleshooting`. Include the `pkill -f lattice && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/ && cp daemon/target/release/lattice ~/.vscode/extensions/lattice.lattice-0.1.0/bin/` deploy sequence from `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy.\n9. Create `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-migration-from-lattice.md`. Migration guide. Required headings: `## Overview`, `## Migration steps` (one ordered checklist), `## Pre-flight checks`, `## Data preservation guarantees`, `## Rollback procedure`, `## Post-migration verification`. Reference the storage migration policy from T03 by heading.\n10. Create `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-benchmark-evaluation-guide.md`. Benchmark how-to. Required headings: `## Overview`, `## Running baseline benchmarks`, `## Running large-repo benchmarks` (cross-link to T80 fixtures), `## Interpreting the metrics report`, `## Regression detection`, `## Initial targets` (the §Measurable Success Criteria initial targets verbatim).\n11. Create `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-extension-review-ui-guide.md`. Extension review UI walkthrough. Required headings: `## Overview`, `## Opening the review panel`, `## Memory inbox`, `## Promotion queue and contradiction queue`, `## Stale view and evidence inspector`, `## Event trace and retrieval explanation`, `## Consolidation, indexing, and graph health`, `## Accept/reject workflow`. Cross-link to T71–T76 file paths.\n12. For every doc, cite spec headings exactly per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Markdown Heading References. Do not duplicate spec content; cite the heading and add interpretation only.\n13. Confirm the MCP contract reference produced by T61 (Phase 8) is linked from the operator guide and the architecture overview. If T61 did not deliver a standalone file, this task documents the link to the relevant section in `mcp.rs` doc-comments or the inline tool documentation.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-successor-architecture-overview.md` — top-level architecture overview.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-model-reference.md` — authoritative memory model reference.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-event-log-design.md` — authoritative event log design.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-design.md` — authoritative consolidation design.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-retrieval-ranking-design.md` — authoritative retrieval and ranking design.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-verification-freshness-design.md` — authoritative verification and freshness design.\n- `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-operator-guide.md` — operator how-to.\n- `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-migration-from-lattice.md` — migration guide.\n- `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-benchmark-evaluation-guide.md` — benchmark + evaluation how-to.\n- `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-extension-review-ui-guide.md` — extension review UI walkthrough.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-successor-architecture-overview.md`\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-model-reference.md`\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-event-log-design.md`\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-design.md`\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-retrieval-ranking-design.md`\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-verification-freshness-design.md`\n- `test -f docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-operator-guide.md`\n- `test -f docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-migration-from-lattice.md`\n- `test -f docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-benchmark-evaluation-guide.md`\n- `test -f docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-extension-review-ui-guide.md`\n- `grep -q '## Overview' docs/architecture/2026-05-16-successor-architecture-overview.md`\n- `grep -q '## Migration steps' docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-migration-from-lattice.md`\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (`wc -l` every doc).\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, no placeholder sections (`coming soon`).\n- Single source of truth: each concept lives in exactly one doc; cross-references use exact `## Heading` anchors per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Markdown Heading References.\n- Naming: doc filenames follow the `YYYY-MM-DD-topic.md` convention already in use in `docs/architecture/`.\n- Doc citation: every doc that depends on the spec cites the spec heading by exact text; every doc that depends on another in this suite cites the target heading by exact text. No vague \"see the architecture docs\" prose.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs, no placeholders).\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] Every spec §Documentation Requirements item is covered by at least one doc in this suite. (The eleventh required item — \"MCP contract reference\" — is produced by T61 in Phase 8 and cross-linked from this suite; if T61 did not produce a standalone file, this task documents the inline location.)\n- [ ] Every doc cross-references the spec by exact heading; nothing duplicates spec content.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every required doc shipped; the runbook + recovery playbook (T86) are the sibling task pair, not deferrals.\n- [ ] After build, deploy per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy procedure (docs do not require deploy, but if any embedded paths change, the binary copies must follow).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":101320,"cache_read_input_tokens":10845,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":101320,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjrTa6YAS1dmMW989ZPauZ","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"2f3debf8-8e1b-4768-b9f2-5ed848461be9","request_id":"req_011Cb7NGicAyFMeCwEAwKwU2","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 10+11+Final task briefs"}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:901:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KGtXP2EMVTtVtg5QavRdVh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018fzsBcFMBkmEMDyc7m4ApV","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R88.md","content":"# R88 — Definition-of-Done gate — shared checklist compliance for the whole fork\n\n**Phase:** Definition-of-Done gate\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R87\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 11: Hardening](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-11-hardening), [§Non-Negotiable Product Properties](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#non-negotiable-product-properties), [§Measurable Success Criteria](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#measurable-success-criteria)\n**Standards reviewed:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); UI specification (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/ui-specification.md`); definition-of-done checklist (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`); execution philosophy (`/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md`).\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis review walks every section of the shared `definition-of-done-checklist.md` against the whole cognitive-workspace fork and certifies that each applicable item is satisfied or explicitly deferred with reason, owner, and target date per the execution philosophy in `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (\"Never defer work you can do now\"). It is the second-to-last gate before R89 final readiness; passing this review means the whole-system delivery meets the cross-cutting \"done means done\" standard that applies regardless of which phase shipped a given artifact. Silent deferrals are not permitted — the `## Explicit Deferrals` section must either be empty (no deferrals) or list every deferral with reason, owner, and target date.\n\n## Inputs to read\n\n- Every artifact from every prior phase task and every prior review (R05 through R87).\n- Shared checklist: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md` — this review walks every section.\n- Shared coding standard: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` §Done means done.\n- Execution philosophy: `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` §Execution Philosophy (\"Never defer work you can do now. ... Never implement a workaround when the real solution exists. ... Stop reasoning about time like a human.\").\n- Spec sections this review enforces: `## Phase 11: Hardening` DoD, `## Non-Negotiable Product Properties`, `## Measurable Success Criteria`.\n\n## Review procedure\n\n1. Open `definition-of-done-checklist.md` and walk it section by section against the fork delivery. Each section below is a heading in the output file and a procedure here.\n2. **Workflow Completion**: Confirm every primary operator workflow works end to end. For the fork, the primary workflows are: (a) the assistant calling MCP tools to plan and apply a change; (b) the operator reviewing the memory inbox, accepting/rejecting promotions and contradictions, inspecting evidence, and triggering on-demand verification; (c) the operator deploying a new daemon binary via the runbook. Confirm both backend and operator-facing UI are complete for every user-visible workflow. Confirm background jobs (consolidation, verification, compaction) are complete.\n3. **Failure Handling**: Confirm validation failures return actionable errors. Confirm permission-denied is not applicable (local-first, no per-user RBAC), but workspace-boundary enforcement is verified by T83. Confirm not-found and conflict states are truthful (e.g. proposal apply on an already-applied proposal returns a clear error per T81). Confirm partial-failure behavior is defined for async paths (consolidation queue, verification jobs). Confirm UI shows loading / empty / success / failure states per R78.\n4. **Security, Tenancy, and Audit**: Confirm access control is local-first; workspace scope is enforced per T83. Confirm destructive actions (memory invalidation, high-scope promotion) require explicit operator confirm per T73. Confirm meaningful state-changing actions create event-log records per Phase 2 + Phase 8. Confirm sensitive data (event payloads with file content) is local-only and not exposed externally.\n5. **Data Integrity and Workflow Controls**: Confirm invariants are enforced at the storage layer (foreign keys on `memory_links`, `memory_evidence`; constraints on verification status enum; uniqueness on event id). Confirm workflow statuses use explicit transition rules (verification status state machine, proposal state machine). Confirm invalid transitions are blocked and tested (T81 idempotency test).\n6. **Observability and Recovery**: Confirm logs and event records provide enough context to debug production failures (T82 recovery tests; T83 workspace-boundary tests emit `security` target events). Confirm critical async paths are idempotent (T81 replay-safe consolidation). Confirm recovery steps exist (T86 recovery playbook). Confirm rollback is defined (T84 migration rollback).\n7. **Performance and Scale**: Confirm the design avoids N+1 and broad scans per spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties (T83 no-broad-fallback test). Confirm pagination / sortable headers are server-side capable for the review UI (R78). Confirm large-repo scale is exercised (T80). Confirm known scale limits are documented (T80 results in `large_repo_results.json`).\n8. **Documentation and Operator Readiness**: Confirm architecture documentation updated for every structural change (T02, T03, T16, T85). Confirm functional documentation reflects every behavior change. Confirm manual documentation (operator guide, runbook, recovery playbook) is updated per T85 + T86. Confirm operator-facing warnings (queue at bound, dropped jobs, broken references) are documented per T76 + T86.\n9. **Verification Evidence**: Confirm unit, integration, and E2E coverage exists. Confirm test commands were executed and results captured (R87 hardening evidence + R79 contract round-trip evidence). Confirm manual verification was captured for UI-heavy changes (R78).\n10. **Explicit Deferrals**: Walk every task brief T01–T86 and every review R05–R87. List every item explicitly deferred with reason, owner, and target date. Per `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` execution philosophy, the expected state is an empty list. Any deferral must be justified or rejected back to the build.\n\n## Required sections in the review output file\n\nThe reviewer writes to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md` with these mandatory headings (one per checklist section from `shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`; each must contain real findings, not \"n/a\"):\n\n- `## Workflow Completion` — confirm assistant workflows, operator review workflows, deploy workflow, and background jobs are all complete end-to-end. Evidence column cites the phase + task that delivered each.\n- `## Failure Handling` — validation failures, permission-denied (not applicable here, document why), not-found / conflict, partial-failure, UI states. Evidence cites the tests + reviews that prove each.\n- `## Security, Tenancy, and Audit` — access control (local-first), workspace scope, destructive-action controls, audit (event log), sensitive data handling. Evidence cites T83 + T73 + Phase 2/8.\n- `## Data Integrity and Workflow Controls` — invariants in storage layer, transition rules, blocked transitions tests. Evidence cites Phase 3 schema + T81 + T82.\n- `## Observability and Recovery` — log/audit context, idempotency, recovery steps, rollback. Evidence cites T81 + T82 + T84 + T86.\n- `## Performance and Scale` — no broad scans, pagination/sort, large-repo scale, documented limits. Evidence cites T80 + T83 + R78.\n- `## Documentation and Operator Readiness` — architecture, functional, manual, operator-facing warnings. Evidence cites T02 + T03 + T16 + T85 + T86.\n- `## Verification Evidence` — unit, integration, E2E, commands executed, manual evidence. Evidence cites R87 + R79 + R78.\n- `## Explicit Deferrals` — MUST be either empty (state explicitly: \"No deferrals. Every spec item shipped in this build per the execution philosophy.\") or list each deferral with: deferred item, reason (must be technically valid, not \"time constraint\"), owner (named individual or role), target date (specific). Per `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md`: \"Never defer work you can do now. ... Offering to 'come back to this later' or 'leave this for a follow-up' is a failure mode.\"\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md` — confirms the review markdown exists.\n- `grep -q '## Workflow Completion' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n- `grep -q '## Failure Handling' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n- `grep -q '## Security, Tenancy, and Audit' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n- `grep -q '## Data Integrity and Workflow Controls' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n- `grep -q '## Observability and Recovery' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n- `grep -q '## Performance and Scale' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n- `grep -q '## Documentation and Operator Readiness' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n- `grep -q '## Verification Evidence' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n- `grep -q '## Explicit Deferrals' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Review markdown file exists at the path verification commands check.\n- [ ] Every one of the nine checklist sections above is present with concrete content (not \"n/a\").\n- [ ] `## Explicit Deferrals` is either empty (with the explicit \"No deferrals.\" statement) or every deferral lists reason + owner + target date — no silent deferrals, no vague \"to be revisited later\" prose.\n- [ ] Every section's evidence column cites the specific task/review/test that satisfies the checklist item.\n- [ ] If any section verdict is FAIL or any deferral cannot meet the reason+owner+date bar, the gate is BLOCK and a follow-up task is opened in this build (never deferred to a future session per `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` execution philosophy).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":135377,"cache_read_input_tokens":10845,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":135377,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjrTa6YAS1dmMW989ZPauZ","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"983c4a68-a9df-4c12-8da3-3966610b92f6","request_id":"req_011Cb7Nnnq1PmkU6diUQFNyf","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 10+11+Final task briefs"}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:904:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KGtXP2EMVTtVtg5QavRdVh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012ffEoGMdEb4EkcctMCv2QH","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R89.md","content":"# R89 — Final readiness review — end-to-end fork acceptance\n\n**Phase:** Final readiness\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R05, R10, R18, R25, R26, R33, R38, R47, R54, R55, R63, R64, R70, R78, R79, R87, R88\n**Spec anchor:** [§Implementation Plan](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#implementation-plan), [§Measurable Success Criteria](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#measurable-success-criteria), [§Risks](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#risks), [§Final Target](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#final-target)\n**Standards reviewed:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); UI specification (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/ui-specification.md`); definition-of-done checklist (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`); execution philosophy (`/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md`).\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis is the final gate before the cognitive-workspace fork is declared shippable. It assembles three matrices that each prior review touched only locally: (1) spec coverage matrix — one row per spec §Phase asserting PASS/PASS-WITH-CAVEATS/BLOCK; (2) measurable success criteria matrix — one row per target from spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial targets, with the evidence file path proving the target was hit; (3) risk controls matrix — one row per risk from spec §Risks asserting the control is implemented and pointing to the artifact that proves it. The review concludes with a single binding `## Ship verdict`: PASS or BLOCK. The verification step runs the full daemon test workspace and the full extension build to confirm the system compiles, lints, tests, and ships clean from a fresh checkout.\n\n## Inputs to read\n\n- Every prior review verdict: R05 (Phase 0), R10 (Phase 1), R18 (Phase 2), R25 (cross-layer contract gate identity+events+memory), R26 (Phase 3), R33 (Phase 4), R38 (Phase 5), R47 (Phase 6), R54 (Phase 7), R55 (cross-layer contract gate memory+verification+retrieval), R63 (Phase 8), R64 (MCP schema regression contract gate), R70 (Phase 9), R78 (Phase 10 frontend), R79 (extension↔daemon contract gate), R87 (Phase 11 hardening+docs), R88 (definition-of-done gate).\n- Every spec §Phase from §Phase 0 through §Phase 11.\n- Spec §Measurable Success Criteria — initial targets list.\n- Spec §Risks — every named risk.\n- Shared standards: `coding.md`, `ui-specification.md`, `definition-of-done-checklist.md`, `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` execution philosophy.\n\n## Review procedure\n\n1. Walk every spec §Phase (0 through 11) and assemble the spec coverage matrix. For each phase, locate the review file that covered it, capture the verdict, and propagate PASS / PASS-WITH-CAVEATS / BLOCK into this matrix. Any BLOCK from a prior review propagates to BLOCK here unless the blocking finding was resolved by a later follow-up task documented in this build.\n2. Walk every target from spec §Measurable Success Criteria → \"Initial targets\":\n   - 30 percent fewer discovery tool calls on benchmark tasks\n   - 40 percent fewer irrelevant file reads\n   - 80 percent memory inclusion precision on curated memory benchmarks\n   - zero trusted display of known contradicted memory\n   - zero trusted display of known stale memory without stale label\n   - 90 percent correct relevant-test recommendation on curated tasks\n   For each, locate the evidence file (typically a benchmark report under `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/` or a test name under `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/` or `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/benchmark_tests.rs`). Record evidence file path + value observed + target met/missed.\n3. Walk every risk from spec §Risks (Opaque Memory Mutation, Ranking Complexity, Event Log Growth, Stale Memory Leakage, Scope Leakage, Overfitting To Current Repo) and confirm the control documented in the spec is implemented and tested. For each, cite the implementation file and the test that proves the control.\n4. Run the full verification suite from a clean state:\n   - `cd daemon && cargo build --release` — full release build.\n   - `cd daemon && cargo test --workspace` — full daemon test workspace.\n   - `cd extension && npm run compile` — extension TypeScript compile.\n   - `cd extension && npm run lint` — extension lint.\n   - `cd extension && npm test` — extension test suite including R79's contract tests.\n   Any failure blocks the ship verdict.\n5. Confirm the deploy sequence from `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy works end-to-end: `pkill -f lattice && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/ && cp daemon/target/release/lattice ~/.vscode/extensions/lattice.lattice-0.1.0/bin/`. Confirm the extension picks up the new binary.\n6. Confirm R88's `## Explicit Deferrals` section is either empty or every deferral meets the reason+owner+date bar; any silent deferral blocks the ship verdict per `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` execution philosophy.\n7. Confirm every spec §Non-Negotiable Product Property is satisfied (cross-reference with R83 workspace-boundary tests, R81 concurrency tests, R82 recovery tests, R87 hardening evidence).\n8. Confirm spec §Final Target is met: \"make a coding agent feel like it is operating in a workspace that remembers accurately.\" This is the qualitative final test — assemble evidence from R70 metrics + R78 frontend + R79 contract round-trips to argue the system delivers on each of the nine final-target bullet points.\n\n## Required sections in the review output file\n\nThe reviewer writes to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R89-final-readiness.md` with these mandatory headings (each must contain real content, not \"n/a\"):\n\n- `## Spec coverage matrix` — one row per spec §Phase (Phase 0 through Phase 11). Columns: phase, review file path, verdict (PASS / PASS-WITH-CAVEATS / BLOCK), notes (cite caveats by review-finding id if any).\n- `## Measurable success criteria` — one row per target from spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial targets (six targets). Columns: target text (verbatim from spec), evidence file path, value observed, met/missed verdict.\n- `## Risk controls in place` — one row per risk from spec §Risks (Opaque Memory Mutation, Ranking Complexity, Event Log Growth, Stale Memory Leakage, Scope Leakage, Overfitting To Current Repo). Columns: risk name, spec-mandated control, implementation file, test file/name that proves the control, verdict.\n- `## Ship verdict` — PASS or BLOCK. If PASS, the verdict line is a single declarative sentence: \"PASS — the cognitive-workspace fork ships.\" If BLOCK, the verdict line lists every blocker by id with a one-sentence summary, and the review opens a follow-up task in this build per `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` execution philosophy.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R89-final-readiness.md` — confirms the review markdown exists.\n- `grep -q '## Spec coverage matrix' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R89-final-readiness.md`\n- `grep -q '## Measurable success criteria' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R89-final-readiness.md`\n- `grep -q '## Risk controls in place' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R89-final-readiness.md`\n- `grep -q '## Ship verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R89-final-readiness.md`\n- `cd daemon && cargo build --release` — release build succeeds.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test --workspace` — full daemon test workspace passes.\n- `cd extension && npm run compile` — extension compile succeeds.\n- `cd extension && npm run lint` — extension lint passes.\n- `cd extension && npm test` — extension test suite (including R79 contract tests) passes.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Review markdown file exists at the path verification commands check.\n- [ ] All four mandatory sections present with concrete content (not \"n/a\").\n- [ ] Every spec §Phase has a row in `## Spec coverage matrix` with a verdict.\n- [ ] Every spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target has a row in `## Measurable success criteria` with an evidence file path and a met/missed verdict.\n- [ ] Every spec §Risk has a row in `## Risk controls in place` with the implementation file and the test that proves the control.\n- [ ] Every verification command was actually executed from a clean checkout and the result captured.\n- [ ] `## Ship verdict` is either an unambiguous PASS or a BLOCK with named blockers.\n- [ ] If verdict is BLOCK, follow-up tasks are opened in this build (never deferred to a future session per `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` execution philosophy — \"Never defer work you can do now\").\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":135377,"cache_read_input_tokens":10845,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":135377,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjrTa6YAS1dmMW989ZPauZ","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"e96dfde1-05a1-44a9-8784-b828da81adec","request_id":"req_011Cb7Nnnq1PmkU6diUQFNyf","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 10+11+Final task briefs"}
