docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:922:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NaxT2HJfaUnYW9Aa3kpoWp","type":"tool_result","content":"# T01 — Phase 0 — Fork-or-extend decision doc with evidence\n\n**Phase:** 0\n**Type:** foundation\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** none\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 0: Fork Foundation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-0-fork-foundation)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task produces the binding fork-or-extend decision that every subsequent task in this build assumes. The spec gates Phase 0 on a \"fork only if necessary\" rule with four named gate conditions; this document evaluates each gate condition against current Lattice code evidence, names a branch or repo, and records the decision. The decision must precede any structural change because `depends_on` chains assume the layout, crate boundaries, and migration policy that this document selects. Without an explicit, evidence-backed decision, later phases would be free to silently diverge.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 0 ends with an explicit fork/extend decision before any structural code changes begin. Fork if any of the following are true: the memory graph schema changes require breaking the existing `memories` table in a way that cannot be migrated without a full rebuild; the identity model requires changing the primary key or graph edge representation in a way that invalidates existing indexed data; the event log requires a new storage file or WAL mode incompatible with the current daemon's SQLite usage; two or more of the above apply and sharing a codebase would require sustained compatibility shims across all phases.\"\n\n> \"If none of those conditions hold, extend in place on a long-lived branch and skip the repo split. Document the decision and the evidence for it before Phase 1 begins.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: none (this is the first task).\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` (current memory schema and storage)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/graph/` (current identity and edge representation)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` (current SQLite usage and WAL mode)\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-structured-memory.md`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-stable-follow-up-handles.md`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-storage-and-search-backends.md`\n  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/context.md` §4 \"Fork-or-extend decision\"\n- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (no broken windows, single source of truth); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/AGENTS.md` (backward compatibility discipline).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md` §Phase 0 in full to internalize the gate conditions verbatim.\n2. Inspect `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/storage.rs` and `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/schema.rs` (or equivalent) and enumerate every column on the `memories` table; record which Phase 3 fields are additive vs. breaking.\n3. Inspect graph primary keys and edge representation in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/graph/`; determine whether the Phase 1 identity model invalidates existing indexes.\n4. Inspect current SQLite connection setup in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` and confirm WAL/journal mode; determine whether a new `events.db` file can coexist without WAL incompatibility.\n5. Evaluate each of the four gate conditions against the evidence and record a `met`/`unmet` verdict per condition with file/line citations.\n6. State the decision (`extend on long-lived branch` or `fork to new repo`) and name the branch or repo (e.g. `feat/cognitive-workspace`).\n7. Document the migration implication of the decision: which existing data must be preserved, which is rewritten, and the rollback path.\n8. List every downstream task that the decision binds (T02 architecture overview, T03 crate boundaries, T04 baselines, all Phase 1 backend tasks).\n9. Save the decision under `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-fork-or-extend-decision.md` with the mandatory headings checked by verification commands.\n\n## Files expected\n--- T19 ---\n# T19 — Phase 3 — Memory schema redesign (classes incl CounterMemory + required fields)\n\n**Phase:** 3\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R18\n**Spec anchor:** [§Memory Graph](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#4-memory-graph)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules.\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task replaces the legacy single-table memory model with a typed memory schema that the rest of Phase 3 builds on. It defines the full memory-class taxonomy (including `CounterMemory` as a first-class class distinct from a `contradicts` link), the SQLite DDL covering every spec-required memory field, the Rust types that mirror the schema, and an architecture doc that records the model authoritatively so later phases (retrieval, consolidation, verification) reference one source of truth. Without this redesign, memory cannot represent claims, evidence, validity conditions, or counter-claims — only loose notes — which violates the spec's core thesis.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Primary memory classes: `Observation`, `Decision`, `Constraint`, `Pattern`, `AntiPattern`, `WorkflowOutcome`, `FailurePattern`, `Procedure`, `Preference`, `ArchitectureInvariant`, `DocsContract`, `OpenQuestion`, `CounterMemory` — a memory record that explicitly asserts a prior memory is wrong or no longer applicable. Distinct from a `contradicts` link: a link connects two existing memories; a CounterMemory is a first-class record authored by an agent or user that carries its own evidence, scope, and verification status and can itself be superseded or invalidated.\"\n\n> \"Each memory record requires: stable id, content, memory class, assertion type, scope: session, branch, repo, user, organization, verification status, confidence and confidence reason, freshness policy, validity conditions, invalidation triggers, provenance events, evidence references, linked files, linked symbols, linked docs, linked tests, linked memories, contradiction links, supersession links, access history, usefulness scores, last verified state.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R18 — the Phase 2 event log is apnd\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T65\"],\n      \"model_class\": \"balanced\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"files_expected\": [\n        \"daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/metrics_surface.rs\",\n        \"daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/metrics_surface_tests.rs\"\n      ],\n      \"verification_commands\": [\n        \"test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/metrics_surface.rs\",\n        \"cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::metrics_surface_tests\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T68\",\n      \"title\": \"Phase 9 — Regression dashboard / CLI report\",\n      \"task_type\": \"backend\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T65\", \"T66\"],\n      \"model_class\": \"balanced\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"files_expected\": [\n        \"daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs\",\n        \"daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/report.rs\",\n        \"daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/report_tests.rs\",\n        \"docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md\"\n      ],\n      \"verification_commands\": [\n        \"test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs\",\n        \"test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md\",\n        \"cd daemon && cargo build --release --bin lattice_report\",\n        \"cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib metrics::report_tests\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T69\",\n      \"title\": \"Phase 9 — Metrics regression coverage tests (success-criteria targets from spec)\",\n      \"task_type\": \"tests\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T65\", \"T66\", \"T67\", \"T68\"],\n      \"model_class\": \"advanced\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"files_expected\": [\n        \"daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/regression_tests.rs\"\n      ],\n      \"verification_commands\": [\n        \"test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/regression_tests.rs\",\n        \"cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib metrics::regression_tests -- --include-ignored\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"R70\",\n      \"title\": \"Tests/Docs review — Phase 9 metrics + evaluation\",\n      \"task_type\": \"review\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T65\", \"T66\", \"T67\", \"T68\", \"T69\"],\n      \"model_class\": \"advanced\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"files_expected\": [\n        \"docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md\"\n      ],\n      \"verification_commands\": [\n        \"test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md\",\n        \"grep -q '## Spec alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md\",\n        \"grep -q '## Success-criteria coverage' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md\",\n        \"grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T71\",\n      \"title\": \"Phase 10 — Extension review-panel scaffolding + JSON-RPC plumbing to new tools\",\n      \"task_type\": \"frontend\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"R70\"],\n      \"model_class\": \"balanced\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"files_expected\": [\n        \"extension/src/review/reviewPanel.ts\",\n        \"extension/src/review/rpcBridge.ts\",\n        \"extension/src/review