docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md:7:> Tool surface discipline: ten new memory tools is a meaningful cognitive load for clients. Before shipping Phase 8, audit whether `propose_memory_evolution` + `apply_memory_evolution` can collapse into a single tool with an `action` parameter, and whether `verify_memory` + `explain_memory` can be unified. The goal is the smallest surface that covers all assistant workflows. Consolidate before stabilizing the MCP contract.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md:15:| Collapse `propose_memory_evolution` and `apply_memory_evolution` into canonical `propose_memory_evolution` with `action` values `propose`, `apply`, and `reject`. | Proposal creation, application, and rejection are one auditable memory-evolution lifecycle. A single tool keeps proposal ids, decision reasons, actor metadata, and transactional update semantics in one contract. | [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface) says to audit whether the pair can collapse and sets the goal as the smallest surface that covers assistant workflows. | `apply_memory_evolution` remains advertised as a deprecated shim in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs`; it forwards to `propose_memory_evolution(action="apply")` and attaches `deprecation_warning`. | Remove no earlier than one full numbered phase cycle after Phase 8 once first-party prompts, fixtures, docs, and cached examples call the canonical action form, following [## Shim removal protocol](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#shim-removal-protocol). |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md:16:| Collapse `verify_memory` and `explain_memory` into canonical `verify_explain_memory` with `mode` values `verify`, `explain`, and `verify_and_explain`. | Verification and explanation share the same evidence checks, status taxonomy, confidence delta, and expansion handle. Keeping two canonical tools would duplicate result semantics and make clients choose between freshness and diagnostics. | [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface) explicitly asks whether `verify_memory` and `explain_memory` can be unified. [## MCP Tool Contract Principles](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles) requires memory-bearing responses to identify evidence strength, verification status, freshness, and explanation metadata. | `verify_memory` and `explain_memory` remain advertised deprecated shims in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs`; each forces the appropriate `mode` and attaches `deprecation_warning`. | Remove no earlier than one full numbered phase cycle after Phase 8 once maintained clients have migrated to `verify_explain_memory`, following [## Shim removal protocol](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#shim-removal-protocol). |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md:23:| `propose_memory_evolution` | `propose_memory_evolution(action="propose")` | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` | Canonical. |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md:24:| `apply_memory_evolution` | `propose_memory_evolution(action="apply")` | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` | Deprecated advertised shim with warning. |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md:25:| `verify_memory` | `verify_explain_memory(mode="verify")` | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` | Deprecated advertised shim with warning. |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md:26:| `explain_memory` | `verify_explain_memory(mode="explain")` | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` | Deprecated advertised shim with warning. |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md:37:| `consolidate_session` and `propose_memory_evolution` | Keep separate. | `consolidate_session` produces proposal ids from event episodes and consolidation categories; `propose_memory_evolution` applies or rejects specific memory-evolution proposals. Generation and decision remain distinct workflow boundaries for auditability. |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md:38:| `get_memory_metrics`, `get_event_trace`, and `get_session_metrics` | Keep separate. | `get_memory_metrics` reports Phase 9 memory/workflow signals with provenance, `get_event_trace` pages event envelopes, and `get_session_metrics` reports live assistant-session MCP metrics. They have different scopes, budgets, and response shapes. |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:41:| `index_status` | Reports current indexing status, graph stats, and language breakdown. | No arguments. | Operational status snapshot. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:42:| `get_session_metrics` | Reports live assistant-session workflow metrics. | No arguments. | Metrics such as tool calls, payload sizes, handle reuse, and automatic memory writes. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | Not self-counted; other calls record generic metrics. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:45:| `list_observations` | Lists stored observations and memories, newest first. | Optional `session_id`, `limit`. | Memory list excluding invalidated records. | Structured response. | `limit` bounds results. | generic events. | Redesigned-with-shim. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:46:| `list_stale_memories` | Lists stale memories likely needing review or refresh. | Optional `query`, `limit`. | Stale memory candidates. | Structured response. | `limit` bounds results. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:51:| `consolidate_session` | Triggers proposal-only session consolidation and returns auditable proposal ids. | `session_id` required; optional `mode`, `budget_ms`, `render_mode`. | Consolidation report with proposals, categories, incomplete flag, and notes. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`. | `budget_ms`; render mode bounds detail. | generic events; `MemoryConsolidated`. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/consolidate_session.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:52:| `get_memory_metrics` | Returns Phase 9 memory and workflow metrics with provenance and honest nulls for unavailable signals. | Optional `scope`, `time_range`, `signals`, `render_mode`. | Metric snapshot with requested signals, values, provenance, per-signal null reasons, and explicit `session_metrics` fallback provenance when the canonical collector had no bounded evidence. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`. | Requested `signals` and render mode bound payload. | generic events. | Stable canonical Phase 9 metrics surface. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_memory_metrics.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/metrics_surface.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:53:| `get_event_trace` | Returns paginated, workspace-bounded event traces for task, session, or workspace scopes. | Optional `task_id`, `session_id`, `workspace_id`, `kinds`, `since`, `until`, `cursor`, `limit`, `render_mode`. | Event page with scope, events, cursor, payloads in full/diagnostic, hashes in diagnostic. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; event expansion handles. | `limit`, cursor pagination, filters, render mode. | generic events; returns event records. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_event_trace.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:56:| `propose_memory_evolution` | Persists, applies, or rejects auditable memory-evolution proposals. | `action` required; proposal actions accept `proposal_id`, `memory_id`, content, links, validity, invalidation, supersession, reason, and actor fields as applicable. | Evolution proposal/result with proposal id, action, proposed memory state, decision metadata, and optional deprecation warning for shimmed calls. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; apply/reject emits consolidation/update lifecycle through memory path. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:57:| `apply_memory_evolution` | Deprecated advertised shim for applying an existing evolution proposal. | `proposal_id` required; optional `reason`, `decided_by`. | Same result as `propose_memory_evolution(action="apply")` plus `deprecation_warning`. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; canonical action path. | Deprecated shim; remove per compatibility policy. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:58:| `verify_explain_memory` | Runs fresh verification checks for a durable memory or explains the last persisted report. | `memory_id` required; optional `mode`, `render_mode`. | Verification status, checks, confidence delta, expansion handle, summary lines, optional diagnostic trace. | `mode=verify/explain/verify_and_explain`; `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; expansion handle. | Render mode bounds detail. | generic events; verification memory retrieval/invalidation as applicable. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:59:| `verify_memory` | Deprecated advertised shim for verification-only mode. | Same as `verify_explain_memory`; shim forces `mode=verify`. | Same response as canonical verify mode plus `deprecation_warning`. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; expansion handle. | Render mode bounds detail. | generic events; canonical mode path. | Deprecated shim; remove per compatibility policy. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:60:| `explain_memory` | Deprecated advertised shim for explanation-only mode. | Same as `verify_explain_memory`; shim forces `mode=explain`. | Same response as canonical explain mode plus `deprecation_warning`. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; expansion handle. | Render mode bounds detail. | generic events; canonical mode path. | Deprecated shim; remove per compatibility policy. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:61:| `list_memory_conflicts` | Lists contradiction and supersession edges anchored on a memory or graph node. | Anchor identity or legacy memory id; optional scope, pagination, and `render_mode`. | Conflict page with anchors, edges, summaries, and pagination. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`. | Pagination and render mode bound payload. | generic events. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/list_memory_conflicts.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:79:Workflow tools use `render=json|markdown|hybrid` for delivery shape and `mode=auto|compact|full` when a workflow bundle supports response density. `get_context_capsule` keeps its older `mode=full|focused` discovery control. Memory v2 administrative tools use `render_mode=compact|full|diagnostic`; `verify_explain_memory` additionally uses `mode=verify|explain|verify_and_explain`.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:85:Workflow responses that return bundles store context handles through `context_cache` and expose `suggested_expand` targets. `expand_context` is the canonical follow-up tool and accepts a prior `handle` plus a `focus` such as a file, symbol, test, memory, or stable identity. Memory-bearing responses expose memory or event expansion handles where useful: `get_task_memory`, `verify_explain_memory`, `get_event_trace`, and `inspect_working_memory` all return handles for focused follow-up.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:93:Other tools expose narrower controls: `limit` bounds list/search/event outputs, `hops` and `max_depth` bound graph traversal, `budget_tokens` bounds `get_task_memory`, `budget_ms` bounds synchronous consolidation, cursor pagination bounds `get_event_trace`, and render modes bound diagnostic detail.
