docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-llm-budgets.md:5:This note defines the default budget, bounded queue, failure, and provenance contract for Phase 6 LLM-driven consolidation jobs: episode summary generation, procedure extraction, contradiction detection, and failure-pattern extraction. `BudgetCatalog` in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/budget.rs` is the canonical source of truth; this document mirrors those defaults for operators.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-llm-budgets.md:16:## Bounded queue depth
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-llm-budgets.md:18:The consolidation queue is globally bounded by `ConsolidationConfig::max_queue_depth`. LLM submission can additionally use a per-kind slice quota through `BoundedJobQueue::with_per_kind_max_depth`. When a slice is full, the daemon drops the incoming job, persists it as `dropped`, emits a `tracing::warn!` with `workspace_id`, `kind`, `current_depth`, and `max_depth`, and writes a `ConsolidationFailed` event with `error_kind = "queue_full"`.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-llm-budgets.md:26:Every successful LLM proposal stores `provenance_json` on `consolidation_proposals`. The record contains `model`, `prompt_sha256`, `response_sha256`, `prompt_token_count`, `response_token_count`, `latency_ms`, and `called_at`. Hashes use SHA-256 over the exact prompt and response bytes, which lets operators verify that a proposal came from the recorded prompt and response without storing either blob in the proposal row.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:9:Legend: `generic events` means the daemon records `ToolCalled` and `ToolResult` when event capture is enabled. `workflow events` means the workflow response also carries the Phase 8 standard sequence `AssistantTaskStarted`, `ToolCalled`, `ContextBundleReturned`, `MemoryRetrieved`, and `PlanCreated` in its workflow event metadata.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:48:| `refresh_memory` | Refreshes memory evidence and metadata while preserving identity and clearing stale state. | `id` required; optional content, type, scope, links, workspace, branch, freshness, confidence. | Updated memory metadata. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; memory update path. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:51:| `consolidate_session` | Triggers proposal-only session consolidation and returns auditable proposal ids. | `session_id` required; optional `mode`, `budget_ms`, `render_mode`. | Consolidation report with proposals, categories, incomplete flag, and notes. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`. | `budget_ms`; render mode bounds detail. | generic events; `MemoryConsolidated`. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/consolidate_session.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:54:| `get_task_memory` | Reads working memory plus relevant durable memory for the current task. | `task_id` required; optional `intent_hint`, `budget_tokens`. | Task memory bundle with inclusion reasons, verification/freshness/conflict state, and expansion handles. | Full structured bundle with memory expansion handles. | `budget_tokens` clips memory payload. | generic events; `MemoryRetrieved`. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_task_memory.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:56:| `propose_memory_evolution` | Persists, applies, or rejects auditable memory-evolution proposals. | `action` required; proposal actions accept `proposal_id`, `memory_id`, content, links, validity, invalidation, supersession, reason, and actor fields as applicable. | Evolution proposal/result with proposal id, action, proposed memory state, decision metadata, and optional deprecation warning for shimmed calls. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; apply/reject emits consolidation/update lifecycle through memory path. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:57:| `apply_memory_evolution` | Deprecated advertised shim for applying an existing evolution proposal. | `proposal_id` required; optional `reason`, `decided_by`. | Same result as `propose_memory_evolution(action="apply")` plus `deprecation_warning`. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; canonical action path. | Deprecated shim; remove per compatibility policy. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md:74:- `MemoryRetrieved`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md:89:- `MemoryConsolidated`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md:97:- `MemoryConsolidated` payloads preserve the proposal id, prior state, proposed state, and a canonical `post_apply_state_hash` so replay can re-apply event data without re-running scanners or LLM calls and still detect divergence deterministically.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md:178:Every durable memory requires evidence. The minimum evidence model is shared across direct memory writes, workflow outcome recording, consolidation proposals, and verification:
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md:206:Phase 7 verifier jobs use the shared workflow database and write `verification_jobs` rows, but verifier outcomes still flow through the proposal runtime rather than direct memory mutation. `mark_verified`, `mark_stale`, and `mark_invalidated` remain proposal kinds so replay, review, and event emission keep one mutation contract instead of giving verification a parallel write path. The `verification_jobs.reason` column remains `TEXT`, but mismatch diagnostics are allowed to store structured JSON payloads such as span-mismatch details so the review surface can distinguish citation drift from missing anchors without inventing a second diagnostics table.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md:208:Phase 7 freshness metadata also stays on the memory row as additive compatibility fields rather than a parallel verification-state table. `expires_at` gives time-bound memories an explicit expiry threshold, while `last_verified_graph_snapshot_id` records which post-index graph snapshot last re-validated the memory. The incremental verifier uses those fields together with `memory_evidence` reference narrowing so graph deltas verify only impacted memories, and successful verification still lands through proposal application instead of direct writes.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md:216:Identity is shared first. Files, symbols, docs, sections, events, memories, tests, and context handles need stable ids that can cross graph rows, event rows, memory evidence, and MCP payloads. Phase 1 formalizes that on top of the current `SymbolId` basis described in [docs/architecture/2026-04-11-stable-follow-up-handles.md#Durable-Identity-Basis](./2026-04-11-stable-follow-up-handles.md#durable-identity-basis).
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:156:Purpose: Own background consolidation jobs, episode summaries, memory promotion proposals, duplicate detection, contradiction detection, supersession proposals, procedure extraction, failure-pattern extraction, and review-queue handoff.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:160:- consolidation job model and lifecycle
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:162:- deterministic proposal generation helpers
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:163:- LLM proposal metadata with model, prompt hash, and response hash
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:166:- replay drivers that rebuild memory state from `MemoryConsolidated` events and verify `post_apply_state_hash` against the reconstructed durable state
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:207:Boundary rationale: Verification consumes graph facts and memory evidence. It writes verification results and events, but retrieval only reads those results; retrieval must not decide trust state itself.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md:25:| `prepare_change` | `additive` | Core workflow remains; later phases add event-backed retrieval, memory evidence, and working-memory details. |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md:38:| `record_workflow_outcome` | `additive` | Stable name; later phases add explicit event ids, memory ids, and proposal metadata. |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-graph-schema.md:293:- `MemoryConsolidated` is reserved for Phase 6 consolidation workflows and is
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-fork-or-extend-decision.md:67:| First-class memory evidence | Additive | Add `memory_evidence`; backfill from `evidence_json` and `provenance_json`. |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md:15:| Collapse `propose_memory_evolution` and `apply_memory_evolution` into canonical `propose_memory_evolution` with `action` values `propose`, `apply`, and `reject`. | Proposal creation, application, and rejection are one auditable memory-evolution lifecycle. A single tool keeps proposal ids, decision reasons, actor metadata, and transactional update semantics in one contract. | [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface) says to audit whether the pair can collapse and sets the goal as the smallest surface that covers assistant workflows. | `apply_memory_evolution` remains advertised as a deprecated shim in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs`; it forwards to `propose_memory_evolution(action="apply")` and attaches `deprecation_warning`. | Remove no earlier than one full numbered phase cycle after Phase 8 once first-party prompts, fixtures, docs, and cached examples call the canonical action form, following [## Shim removal protocol](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#shim-removal-protocol). |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md:37:| `consolidate_session` and `propose_memory_evolution` | Keep separate. | `consolidate_session` produces proposal ids from event episodes and consolidation categories; `propose_memory_evolution` applies or rejects specific memory-evolution proposals. Generation and decision remain distinct workflow boundaries for auditability. |
