4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"1cb8777f-e882-4413-87c0-cfea5424ca22","timestamp":"2026-05-17T02:49:46.880Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are writing markdown task brief files for a build harness. Do NOT implement the feature itself — just write the brief markdown files.\n\nRepo root: /home/pete/cadres/lattice\nSpec: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md  (READ Phases 10 and 11 + §Human Review Surface + §Documentation Requirements + §Testing Requirements + §Measurable Success Criteria + §Risks)\nContext: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/context.md\nTasks JSON: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks.json\nShared standards: /home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md AND /home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/ui-specification.md (READ FOR T71–T77 — frontend tasks must honor this) AND /home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md (READ FOR R88 — that review walks the entire checklist).\n\nWrite these 19 files at `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/<TASK_ID>.md`:\n\nT71, T72, T73, T74, T75, T76, T77, R78, R79, T80, T81, T82, T83, T84, T85, T86, R87, R88, R89\n\n**Use the same template structure as prior agents.**\n\nFor frontend tasks (T71–T77), the \"Coding-standard checks\" section MUST add a \"UI specification\" subsection covering:\n- All user-facing strings via `i18n.t(...)` (no inline literals).\n- All modals via native `<dialog>` (no `window.confirm/prompt/alert`).\n- All mutation handlers use `try/catch` with `parseApiError(e)` + `toast.error(...)` if applicable to extension context — for VS Code extension, use `vscode.window.showErrorMessage(err.message)` where `parseApiError` does not apply.\n- All ID inputs use `SearchableSelect` (where applicable to VS Code webview UI; for tree views use `vscode.window.showQuickPick` patterns).\n- Sortable tables use `SortableHeader` + `useTableSort` (where applicable).\n- Status badges + loading + empty + error states for every interactive surface.\n\n**Task-specific guidance:**\n\n- T71 — extension review-panel scaffolding: register a new webview view contribution under existing `viewsContainers.activitybar.lattice` in `extension/package.json`. RPC bridge translates tool responses into typed UI state. Set up i18n with at least `en.json`.\n- T72 — memory inbox: list view with filters (status, scope, class), status badges (verified/unverified/in_review/stale/contradicted/superseded/expired/invalidated).\n- T73 — promotion queue + contradiction queue with accept/reject. Dialogs are native `<dialog>` per ui-specification.md.\n- T74 — stale memory view + evidence inspector + verification trigger that calls `verify_memory` (new tool from Phase 8).\n- T75 — event trace view + retrieval explanation view (shows ranking scores + reasons from Phase 4 diagnostic mode).\n- T76 — consolidation queue + indexing health + workspace graph health.\n- T77 — extension UI smoke tests via VS Code test runner (`npm test` → `node ./out/test/runTest.js`). Tests cover at least: extension activates, review panel registers, each subview renders without throwing.\n- R78 — Phase 10 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## UI-specification compliance` (walk the ui-specification.md sections explicitly), `## i18n coverage`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- R79 — contract gate Extension ↔ Daemon. Required headings: `## Contract surfaces`, `## Round-trip evidence`, `## Schema surfaces`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`. New file `extension/src/test/contract.test.ts`.\n- T80 — large-repo performance tests: fixtures from T66, P99 budgets from Phases 1 and 2 verified at scale.\n- T81 — concurrency tests: parallel sessions, write contention, replay-safe execution.\n- T82 — recovery + corruption: corrupted event payloads, partial snapshots, replay-from-snapshot.\n- T83 — partial-index handling + workspace-boundary tests (per spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties \"no silent broad workspace reads\").\n- T84 — migration tests + MCP schema compatibility regression (covers backward-compat shims from R64).\n- T85 — documentation suite. Required docs from spec §Documentation Requirements:\n  - successor architecture overview\n  - MCP contract reference (was T61)\n  - memory model reference\n  - event log design\n  - consolidation design\n  - retrieval/ranking design\n  - verification/freshness design\n  - operator guide\n  - migration guide from Lattice\n  - benchmark/evaluation guide\n  - extension review UI guide\n- T86 — operator runbook + recovery playbook. Includes deploy sequence: `pkill -f lattice && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/ && cp daemon/target/release/lattice ~/.vscode/extensions/lattice.lattice-0.1.0/bin/` from `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy. Includes replay-from-snapshot procedure.\n- R87 — Phase 11 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Doc coverage matrix` (one row per required doc from spec §Documentation Requirements), `## Hardening evidence`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- R88 — definition-of-done gate. Required headings (one per checklist section from `shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`):\n  - `## Workflow Completion`\n  - `## Failure Handling`\n  - `## Security, Tenancy, and Audit`\n  - `## Data Integrity and Workflow Controls`\n  - `## Observability and Recovery`\n  - `## Performance and Scale`\n  - `## Documentation and Operator Readiness`\n  - `## Verification Evidence`\n  - `## Explicit Deferrals` — this MUST be either empty (no deferrals) or list each deferral with reason + owner + target date per the execution philosophy in `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md`. No silent deferrals.\n- R89 — final readiness review. Required headings:\n  - `## Spec coverage matrix` — one row per spec §Phase, status PASS/PASS-WITH-CAVEATS/BLOCK.\n  - `## Measurable success criteria` — one row per target from spec §Measurable Success Criteria (initial targets); evidence file path.\n  - `## Risk controls in place` — one row per risk from spec §Risks; control implementation evidence.\n  - `## Ship verdict` — PASS or BLOCK.\n\nR89 verification includes a full `cargo test --workspace` + extension compile/lint/test.\n\nRead the spec yourself for exact text. Quote it. Read ui-specification.md and definition-of-done-checklist.md sections relevant to the tasks you write.\n\nFor each task: 5-10 concrete steps, exact file paths from tasks.json, exact verification commands from tasks.json.\n\nWrite all 19 files, then report file count + first 3 paths confirmed. Do NOT modify tasks.json, context.md, or plan.md. Do NOT implement any code in daemon/ or extension/.","agentId":"a78780aeb6875bd27","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 19 task brief files written successfully.\n\n**File count:** 19 (T71, T72, T73, T74, T75, T76, T77, R78, R79, T80, T81, T82, T83, T84, T85, T86, R87, R88, R89).\n\n**First 3 paths confirmed:**\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T71.md`\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T72.md`\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T73.md`\n\n**Summary of coverage:**\n- **T71–T76** (frontend): each task brief follows the prior-agent template (Goal, Spec excerpts, Inputs, Steps, Files expected, Verification, Coding-standard checks with UI-specification subsection, Definition of done). Every frontend brief honors the mandated UI-spec subsection covering i18n via `i18n.t(...)`, native `<dialog>` modals (no `window.confirm/prompt/alert`), `try/catch` with `vscode.window.showErrorMessage(err.message)` (the VS Code analogue to `parseApiError + toast.error`), `vscode.window.showQuickPick` for ID inputs, sortable headers / pagination, and loading/empty/error/badge states for every interactive surface.\n- **T77** (extension UI smoke tests): VS Code test runner via `node ./out/test/runTest.js`; covers activation, view registration, and per-subview render under happy/empty/error.\n- **R78** (Phase 10 frontend review): all required headings (Spec alignment, Coding-standard alignment, UI-specification compliance walking ui-specification.md sections explicitly, i18n coverage, Findings, Verdict).\n- **R79** (Extension↔Daemon contract gate): introduces `extension/src/test/contract.test.ts`; required headings (Contract surfaces, Round-trip evidence, Schema surfaces, Findings, Verdict).\n- **T80–T84** (Phase 11 hardening tests): large-repo perf (with P99 budgets from Phases 1+2), concurrency (parallel sessions / write contention / replay-safe), recovery + corruption, partial-index + workspace-boundary (per spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties), migration + MCP schema compat regression (uses R64 shims).\n- **T85** (documentation suite): all eleven required docs from spec §Documentation Requirements.\n- **T86** (runbook + recovery playbook): quotes the `pkill -f lattice && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/ && cp daemon/target/release/lattice ~/.vscode/extensions/lattice.lattice-0.1.0/bin/` sequence from `lattice/CLAUDE.md` and documents the replay-from-snapshot procedure validated by T82.\n- **R87** (Phase 11 hardening + docs review): required headings including Doc coverage matrix (one row per required doc from spec §Documentation Requirements) and Hardening evidence.\n- **R88** (Definition-of-Done gate): all nine checklist sections from `shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`; `## Explicit Deferrals` must be empty or list each deferral with reason+owner+target-date per the execution philosophy in `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md`.\n- **R89** (Final readiness review): required matrices (Spec coverage by phase, Measurable success criteria with evidence file paths, Risk controls in place with implementation+test evidence), plus a binding Ship verdict (PASS or BLOCK). Verification runs full `cargo test --workspace` and extension compile/lint/test.\n\nNo code in `daemon/` or `extension/` was modified. `tasks.json`, `context.md`, and `plan.md` were not modified."}],"totalDurationMs":987098,"totalTokens":160303,"totalToolUseCount":45,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":825,"cache_read_input_tokens":158112,"output_tokens":1365,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":825},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1365,"cache_read_input_tokens":158112,"cache_creation_input_tokens":825,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":825,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":15,"searchCount":2,"bashCount":9,"editFileCount":19,"linesAdded":1605,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
